PAGE  001   ASMPATCH          



00001                     NAM    ASMPATCH 
00002                     OPT    O,NOM,NOP  
00003              *THIS PROGRAM PATCHES THE M6800 ASSEMBLER
00004              *TO REQUEST THE USER TO SELECT IF OUTPUT IS 
00005              *TO BE SENT THE PRINTER DEVICE USING THE 
00006              * PROM DRIVER
00007              *
00008              *  From Bitsaver's manual
00009              *  M6800_Co-Resident_Assembler_Reference_Manual_1976
00010              *  Modified to work with FDOS-II under SimH
00011              *  by Roberto Sancho, Mar/26
00012              *
00013      0000    PASS   EQU    0 
00014      E047    XSTACK EQU    $E047 
00015      E00C    AECHO  EQU    $E00C    ECHO ON/OFF FLAG =0 -> ECHO,  
00016      E014    ATOPM  EQU    $E014    ADDRESS OF TOP MEMORY. 
00017      011E    XDATA  EQU    $11E     asmb console string out
00018      011B    XCIE   EQU    $11B     asmb console in char
00019      0133    XHEAD  EQU    $133     asmb string out (w/leading <C 
00020      0136    XLINE  EQU    $136     asmb string out
00021      EEEF    LDATA  EQU    $EEEF    printer string out (w/leading 
00022      EEF1    LDATA1 EQU    $EEF1    printer string out
00023      0100    ASMB   EQU    $100     assembler cold start
00024      0301    ENDSTB EQU    $301     default end-of-symbol table a 
00025              *
00026 0020                ORG    $20      assembler entry point from FD 
00027              *
00028 0020 FE E014        LDX    ATOPM    get top of ram
00029 0023 FF 0301        STX    ENDSTBL  set end-of-symbol table addre 
00030 0026 8E E047        LDS    #XSTACK 
00031 0029 96 00          LDA A  PASS 
00032 002B 81 09          CMP A  #$9      OBJECT ONLY?
00033 002D 27 1A          BEQ    ASM      YES
00034 002F CE 005A TOP    LDX    #MSG 
00035 0032 BD 011E        JSR    XDATA 
00036 0035 CE 0000        LDX    #0 
00037 0038 09      DELAY  DEX             
00038 0039 26 FD          BNE    DELAY 
00039 003B 7F E00C        CLR    AECHO    set echo on for user typed ch 
00040 003E BD 011B        JSR    XCIE 
00041 0041 81 59          CMP A  #'Y 
00042 0043 27 07          BEQ    PRNTR 
00043 0045 81 4E          CMP A  #'N 
00044 0047 26 E6          BNE    TOP 
00045 0049 7E 0100 ASM    JMP    ASMB 
00046 004C CE EEEF PRNTR  LDX    #LDATA 
00047 004F FF 0134        STX    XHEAD+1 
00048 0052 CE EEF1        LDX    #LDATA1 
00049 0055 FF 0137        STX    XLINE+1 
00050 0058 20 EF          BRA    ASM 
00051 005A 50      MSG    FCC    /PRINTER?/
      005B 52      
      005C 49      
      005D 4E      
      005E 54      
      005F 45      
      0060 52      
      0061 3F      
00052 0062 04             FCB    4 
00053                     END             

